Alembic migrations for the Lunch App backend.

This app talks to SQLite with plain sqlite3 + hand-written SQL (see
lunchapp/repositories/, lunchapp/core/database.py) -- there is no SQLAlchemy
ORM layer here. Alembic is used purely as a migration *runner*; SQLAlchemy is
only present because Alembic depends on it for its Engine/connection
handling. `target_metadata` in env.py is intentionally None: there is nothing
to autogenerate against.

Existing databases (dev and any deployed one) were bootstrapped by
lunchapp.core.database.Database.init_schema(), which the app still calls on
every boot (see run.py) and will keep doing so -- this migration setup does
not replace that, it sits alongside it. The single baseline revision
(24ac7b783b53) exists only so future schema changes have an Alembic history
to build on, instead of appending another branch to
Database._migrate_columns().

Going forward, when a schema change is needed:

    alembic revision -m "add whatever_column to whatever_table"

...then fill in upgrade()/downgrade() with raw SQL via op.execute(...),
matching the style already used in core/database.py. Do NOT also add the
same change to Database._migrate_columns() -- pick one system per change
(new changes go through Alembic; the ad-hoc bootstrap stays frozen at what
it already covers).

To run migrations: `alembic upgrade head` (reads the DB path from
lunchapp.Config.DB_PATH, or override with the LUNCH_DB_PATH env var).
